      "id": 1,
      "text": "Grass Ranch Colony was established in 1990 as a daughter colony divided from the nearby Platte Hutterite Colony.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grass_ranch_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community belongs to the Schmiedeleut Group 2 tradition of Hutterian Brethren, a communal Anabaptist Christian sect.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grass_ranch_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Residents of Grass Ranch Colony emphasize shared property, pacifism, and collective labor in line with 16th-century Anabaptist principles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grass_ranch_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Grass Ranch Colony is composed exclusively of Hutterite residents who live in communal arrangements with multi-generational families.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grass_ranch_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The colony's self-sustaining lifestyle relies on ranching and farming activities within the central South Dakota prairie landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grass_ranch_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Severe blizzards and periodic droughts in the Great Plains influence the agricultural adaptations used at Grass Ranch Colony.",
